sts. The screen check certifies\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:23:   that exact template, and any template change fails the tests until it is re-certified by a new screen run and a new format\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:26:**Revision 5 answers `codex-r76d.md`:** no text may be clipped.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:30:- A clipping copy is added as a negative page.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:33:- the screen check compares the whole page's visible text, header and every card, with a frozen list; any text outside a known place\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:40:- the screen check compares every visible text of each checked card with a frozen list, in order and grouped by evidence, so an\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:42:- each dated card is frozen from its own dated package;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:48:- the escaping is written out as literal JSON escapes, with the charset and the CSP first in the file;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:50:- the screen check compares the expanded `v8` card with frozen expected entries;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:55:screen check: a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a forecast and history, where only the\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:62:  - the package gains that page (format 2);\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:105:    `content` property anywhere, so every word a reader sees is a text node the screen check can read. It clips no text: none of\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:118:**What the page shows,** in package order. Each shown value sits in an element with a fixed class, so the screen check can read it:\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:162:| `release_check.py` pins `hivemind-release/1`; its helpers that forge data refresh only the data hash | the pin becomes `/2`. The forging helpers also regenerate `index.html = render_page(forged data)` and its hash, so a forged forecast still reaches the store comparison and is refused there, with its exact reason |\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:167:2. **Escaping.**\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:179:     screen run certifies it. A change to any part of the page fails this until it is re-certified.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:190:- `render_page` not escaping `<`;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:197:## 6. The $0 screen check (`release_screen.mjs`, run once)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:202:  the slice-1 command under format 2.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:215:**Expected values, frozen before the run.** `release_screen.mjs` reads `screen-expected.json`. It is written before the first screen\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:218:- `old-3/package-2026-08-25` for `old-3/v36` (at that day it asks whether NVIDIA will begin shipping Rubin Ultra);\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:232:- **Not clipped.**\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:237:  - Any clipped text fails the page, whatever its content.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:238:- **Readable.** Each kept text's contrast ratio is at least 4.5:1, computed (WCAG relative luminance) between its element's computed\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:243:- **What must match.** The read page must equal the frozen page exactly: collapsed, then with the checked card expanded, then after\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:250:- **Collapsed:** the whole read page equals the frozen page. The `v8` card reads \"How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:252:- **With `v8` expanded:** the whole read page equals the frozen page with `v8`'s 1,284 groups. The full Morningstar quote and its\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:253:  attribution are included, and \"Bullish\" appears only where a frozen source text holds it.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:260:- the whole read page, collapsed and with the card expanded, equals the frozen page from that dated package. The card holds its\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:270:- **clipped:** quotes held to one line (`white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis` added through the script's\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:271:  inline style on each quote) fail the not-clipped rule at 390 px, although their text is identical;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:272:- **clipping wrapper:** each quote placed inside a one-line wrapper (`contain: paint; height: 1.5em`), the quote itself wrapping\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:273:  normally, fails the clipping-ancestor rule at 390 px;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:275:  script's inline style) fails the contrast rule, although its text, box and opacity pass;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:277:  `rgb(15, 20, 13)`) inside the light card fails the contrast rule.\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:279:**The escaping screen.** The fixture page of test 2, with that evidence expanded, shows the exact quote as text and has no `img`\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:298:  - with `v8` expanded, the whole read page, with the not-clipped rule, equals the frozen expanded page;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
