{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/release.py | sed -n '489,600p'\nnl -ba tests/test_release.py | sed -n '751,875p'\"","aggregated_output":"   489\t    ':root{--paper:#f5f2eb;--wash:#ebe9e2;--rule:#dfddd6;--ink:#0f140d;--ink-2:#393d36;--ink-3:#6a6c65;color-scheme:light dark}'\n   490\t    '@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){:root{--paper:#0f140d;--wash:#1b2018;--rule:#393d36;--ink:#f5f2eb;--ink-2:#dfddd6;--ink-3:#9f9f98}}'\n   491\t    '*{box-sizing:border-box}'\n   492\t    'body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:15px/1.5 \"Helvetica Neue\",Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif}'\n   493\t    'main{max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 16px 64px}'\n   494\t    '#fallback{max-width:860px;margin:24px auto;padding:0 16px;color:var(--ink-2)}'\n   495\t    '.release-title{font-size:22px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 4px}'\n   496\t    '.release-day,.release-counts{margin:0;color:var(--ink-3);font-size:13px}'\n   497\t    '.release-header{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);padding-bottom:16px;margin-bottom:8px}'\n   498\t    '.question{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);padding:16px 0}'\n   499\t    '.question-text{font-size:16px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}'\n   500\t    '.question-status{display:inline-block;margin:0 12px 0 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--ink-3);text-transform:none}'\n   501\t    '.question-forecast,.question-answer{display:inline-block;margin:0;font-size:13px;padding:1px 8px;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:999px;background:var(--wash)}'\n   502\t    '.evidence{margin-top:10px}'\n   503\t    '.evidence-count{cursor:pointer;font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2)}'\n   504\t    '.evidence-none{margin:10px 0 0;font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-3)}'\n   505\t    '.evidence-list{margin:8px 0 0;padding-left:20px}'\n   506\t    '.evidence-item{margin:0 0 14px}'\n   507\t    '.evidence-summary{margin:0 0 4px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}'\n   508\t    '.evidence-quote{margin:0 0 4px;padding-left:10px;border-left:2px solid var(--rule);color:var(--ink-2);overflow-wrap:anywhere}'\n   509\t    '.evidence-meta{margin:0 0 4px;font-size:12px;color:var(--ink-3);overflow-wrap:anywhere}'\n   510\t    '.source-list{margin:0;padding-left:16px;font-size:12px;color:var(--ink-3)}'\n   511\t    '.source>span{overflow-wrap:anywhere;margin-right:12px}'\n   512\t)\n   513\t\n   514\tPAGE_SCRIPT = (\n   515\t    \"(function(){'use strict';\"\n   516\t    \"var data=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('release-data').textContent);\"\n   517\t    \"var root=document.getElementById('release');\"\n   518\t    \"function el(tag,cls,text){var e=document.createElement(tag);if(cls){e.className=cls;}if(text!==undefined){e.textContent=text;}return e;}\"\n   519\t    \"function piece(e){var item=el('li','evidence-item');\"\n   520\t    \"item.appendChild(el('p','evidence-summary',e.one_line));\"\n   521\t    \"item.appendChild(el('blockquote','evidence-quote',e.quote));\"\n   522\t    \"item.appendChild(el('p','evidence-meta',e.tier+' \\\\u00b7 '+e.speaker+' \\\\u00b7 original: '+e.original_who+(e.original_day?', '+e.original_day:'')));\"\n   523\t    \"var sources=el('ul','source-list');\"\n   524\t    \"e.sources.forEach(function(s){var row=el('li','source');\"\n   525\t    \"row.appendChild(el('span','source-title',s.title));row.appendChild(el('span','source-publisher',s.publisher));\"\n   526\t    \"row.appendChild(el('span','source-day',s.day));row.appendChild(el('span','source-address',s.uri));sources.appendChild(row);});\"\n   527\t    \"item.appendChild(sources);return item;}\"\n   528\t    \"var counts={number:0,event:0,yes_no:0};data.questions.forEach(function(q){counts[q['class']]+=1;});\"\n   529\t    \"var header=el('header','release-header');header.appendChild(el('h1','release-title','Hivemind release'));\"\n   530\t    \"header.appendChild(el('p','release-day','As of '+data.as_of));\"\n   531\t    \"header.appendChild(el('p','release-counts',counts.number+' number questions \\\\u00b7 '+counts.event+' event questions \\\\u00b7 '+counts.yes_no+' Yes/No questions'));\"\n   532\t    \"root.appendChild(header);\"\n   533\t    \"if(!data.questions.length){root.appendChild(el('p','release-empty','No questions as of '+data.as_of));}\"\n   534\t    \"data.questions.forEach(function(q){var card=el('article','question');card.dataset.id=q.id;\"\n   535\t    \"card.appendChild(el('h2','question-text',q.question));card.appendChild(el('p','question-status',q.open?'Open':'Closed'));\"\n   536\t    \"if(q['class']==='number'){card.appendChild(el('p','question-forecast',q.forecast));}\"\n   537\t    \"else{card.appendChild(el('p','question-answer',q.answer===null?'Not yet answered':'Answer: '+q.answer));}\"\n   538\t    \"var n=q.evidence.length;\"\n   539\t    \"if(!n){card.appendChild(el('p','evidence-none','No evidence in force'));}\"\n   540\t    \"else{var details=el('details','evidence');details.appendChild(el('summary','evidence-count',n+(n===1?' piece of evidence':' pieces of evidence')));\"\n   541\t    \"var list=null;details.addEventListener('toggle',function(){if(details.open&&!list){list=el('ol','evidence-list');\"\n   542\t    \"q.evidence.forEach(function(e){list.appendChild(piece(e));});details.appendChild(list);}});card.appendChild(details);}\"\n   543\t    \"root.appendChild(card);});\"\n   544\t    \"var fallback=document.getElementById('fallback');fallback.parentNode.removeChild(fallback);\"\n   545\t    \"})();\"\n   546\t)\n   547\t\n   548\tPAGE_CSP = (\"default-src 'none'; script-src {script}; style-src {style}; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; connect-src 'none'; \"\n   549\t            \"base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'\")\n   550\tEMBED_ESCAPED = ('<', '>', '&', chr(0x2028), chr(0x2029))\n   551\t\n   552\t\n   553\tdef _source_hash(text):\n   554\t    return \"'sha256-\" + base64.b64encode(hashlib.sha256(text.encode('utf-8')).digest()).decode('ascii') + \"'\"\n   555\t\n   556\t\n   557\tdef embed(data_bytes):\n   558\t    \"\"\"The data file's text with `<`, `>`, `&`, U+2028 and U+2029 replaced by their six-character JSON escapes: still the same JSON,\n   559\t    and unable to close or comment out the block it sits in.\"\"\"\n   560\t    text = data_bytes.decode('utf-8')\n   561\t    for character in EMBED_ESCAPED:\n   562\t        text = text.replace(character, chr(92) + f'u{ord(character):04x}')\n   563\t    return text\n   564\t\n   565\t\n   566\tDATA_PLACEHOLDER = '@@RELEASE_DATA@@'\n   567\t\n   568\t\n   569\tdef page_template():\n   570\t    \"\"\"The whole reader's page with its one data placeholder: charset and CSP first; the CSP admits only this template's own script and\n   571\t    style and no connection, image, font, base or form target. Its sha256 is pinned in the tests.\"\"\"\n   572\t    csp = PAGE_CSP.format(script=_source_hash(PAGE_SCRIPT), style=_source_hash(PAGE_STYLE))\n   573\t    return ('<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\"en\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\\n'\n   574\t            f'<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Security-Policy\" content=\"{csp}\">\\n'\n   575\t            '<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\\n<title>Hivemind release</title>\\n'\n   576\t            f'<style>{PAGE_STYLE}</style>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n'\n   577\t            '<p id=\"fallback\">This release page needs JavaScript to show its questions.</p>\\n<main id=\"release\"></main>\\n'\n   578\t            f'<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"release-data\">{DATA_PLACEHOLDER}</script>\\n'\n   579\t            f'<script>{PAGE_SCRIPT}</script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n')\n   580\t\n   581\t\n   582\tdef render_page(data_bytes):\n   583\t    \"\"\"The reader's page: the pinned template split once at its placeholder, with the escaped data inserted.\"\"\"\n   584\t    before, after = page_template().split(DATA_PLACEHOLDER)\n   585\t    return (before + embed(data_bytes) + after).encode('utf-8')\n   586\t\n   587\t\n   588\t# ---------- the report\n   589\t\n   590\tdef withheld_unresolved(views_db, data):\n   591\t    \"\"\"For the release report only: the number questions whose ladder does not resolve to bands, with the reason and whether the\n   592\t    view has a key. Withheld like every number question; this list never enters the package.\"\"\"\n   593\t    out = []\n   594\t    for question in data['questions']:\n   595\t        if question['class'] != 'number':\n   596\t            continue\n   597\t        bands, reason = service.ladder_bands(store.rungs_of(views_db, question['id']))\n   598\t        if bands is None:\n   599\t            out.append({'id': question['id'], 'reason': reason, 'has_key': key_measure(views_db, question['id'], data['as_of']) is not None})\n   600\t    return out\n   751\t\n   752\t# ---------- slice 2: the reader's page (RELEASE-PAGE.md revision 7)\n   753\t\n   754\timport base64  # noqa: E402\n   755\timport re  # noqa: E402\n   756\t\n   757\tNETWORK_APIS = ('fetch', 'XMLHttpRequest', 'WebSocket', 'EventSource', 'sendBeacon', 'import(', 'Worker', 'innerHTML', 'outerHTML',\n   758\t                'insertAdjacentHTML', 'document.write', 'eval(', 'Function(', \"createElement('a')\", 'href', 'src')\n   759\tCLIPPING_PROPERTIES = ('content', 'overflow', 'overflow-x', 'overflow-y', 'clip', 'clip-path', 'contain', 'text-overflow', 'line-clamp',\n   760\t                       '-webkit-line-clamp', 'max-height', 'opacity', 'visibility')\n   761\t\n   762\t\n   763\tdef test_26_the_page_is_a_pure_function_of_the_data_with_literal_escapes():\n   764\t    \"\"\"RELEASE-PAGE.md §5 tests 1 and 2: the same data gives the same page; <, >, &, U+2028 and U+2029 become their six-character\n   765\t    JSON escapes, so the data block cannot close or comment out, and it parses back to the same data.\"\"\"\n   766\t    hostile = '</script><img src=x onerror=alert(1)> & a line' + chr(0x2028) + 'break' + chr(0x2029) + '<!--'\n   767\t    payload = json.dumps({'quote': hostile}, ensure_ascii=False).encode()\n   768\t    page = release.render_page(payload)\n   769\t    assert page == release.render_page(payload)\n   770\t    block = page.decode().split('<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"release-data\">')[1].split('</script>')[0]\n   771\t    backslash = chr(92)\n   772\t    assert block == payload.decode().replace('<', backslash + 'u003c').replace('>', backslash + 'u003e').replace('&', backslash + 'u0026') \\\n   773\t        .replace(chr(0x2028), backslash + 'u2028').replace(chr(0x2029), backslash + 'u2029')\n   774\t    assert '</script' not in block and '<!--' not in block and json.loads(block) == {'quote': hostile}\n   775\t    assert page.decode().count('<script') == 2\n   776\t\n   777\t\n   778\tdef test_27_the_template_has_no_network_code_drawn_text_or_clipping():\n   779\t    \"\"\"RELEASE-PAGE.md §5 test 3: the script uses no network or markup-writing API and makes no link; the stylesheet draws no text and\n   780\t    clips nothing; the CSP is exactly the designed policy with the hashes of the template's own script and style; charset and CSP\n   781\t    come first.\"\"\"\n   782\t    for api in NETWORK_APIS:\n   783\t        assert api not in release.PAGE_SCRIPT, api\n   784\t    for name in CLIPPING_PROPERTIES:\n   785\t        assert not re.search(r'(?<![-\\w])' + re.escape(name) + r'\\s*:', release.PAGE_STYLE), name\n   786\t    assert 'nowrap' not in release.PAGE_STYLE\n   787\t    digest = lambda text: \"'sha256-\" + base64.b64encode(hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).digest()).decode() + \"'\"\n   788\t    csp = (f\"default-src 'none'; script-src {digest(release.PAGE_SCRIPT)}; style-src {digest(release.PAGE_STYLE)}; img-src 'none'; \"\n   789\t           \"font-src 'none'; connect-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'\")\n   790\t    template = release.page_template()\n   791\t    assert template.startswith('<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\"en\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\\n'\n   792\t                               f'<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Security-Policy\" content=\"{csp}\">\\n')\n   793\t    assert template.count(release.DATA_PLACEHOLDER) == 1\n   794\t\n   795\t\n   796\tdef test_28_the_package_page_must_be_the_page_of_its_data(stores, tmp_path):\n   797\t    \"\"\"RELEASE-PAGE.md §5 test 4: a page changed by one byte, or with a fetch added and its CSP and hashes updated, is refused because\n   798\t    it is not render_page(data); a correct page with only its manifest hash wrong is refused for that reason; a fourth file is\n   799\t    refused.\"\"\"\n   800\t    out = tmp_path / 'release'\n   801\t    build_package(stores, out)\n   802\t    assert check(stores, out)['fields_compared'] == FIXTURE_COUNTS['fields_compared']\n   803\t\n   804\t    def copy_with(name, page=None, page_hash=None):\n   805\t        target = tmp_path / name\n   806\t        shutil.copytree(out, target)\n   807\t        if page is not None:\n   808\t            (target / release.PAGE_FILE).write_bytes(page)\n   809\t        manifest = json.loads((target / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())\n   810\t        manifest['page_sha256'] = page_hash or hashlib.sha256((target / release.PAGE_FILE).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n   811\t        (target / release.MANIFEST_FILE).write_text(json.dumps(manifest))\n   812\t        return target\n   813\t\n   814\t    original = (out / release.PAGE_FILE).read_bytes()\n   815\t    one_byte = copy_with('one-byte', original.replace(b'needs JavaScript', b'needs Javascript'))\n   816\t    refused_with(lambda: check(stores, one_byte), 'the page is not the page made from its data')\n   817\t    script = release.PAGE_SCRIPT\n   818\t    added = script.replace(\"(function(){'use strict';\", \"(function(){'use strict';fetch('http://127.0.0.1:59999/library').catch(function(){});\")\n   819\t    digest = lambda text: \"'sha256-\" + base64.b64encode(hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).digest()).decode() + \"'\"\n   820\t    fetching = original.decode().replace(script, added).replace(digest(script), digest(added)).encode()\n   821\t    assert fetching != original\n   822\t    refused_with(lambda: check(stores, copy_with('fetching', fetching)), 'the page is not the page made from its data')\n   823\t    wrong_hash = copy_with('wrong-hash', page_hash='0' * 64)\n   824\t    refused_with(lambda: check(stores, wrong_hash), 'the manifest page_sha256 does not match the page')\n   825\t    fourth = tmp_path / 'fourth'\n   826\t    shutil.copytree(out, fourth)\n   827\t    (fourth / 'extra.html').write_text('<p>x</p>')\n   828\t    refused_with(lambda: check(stores, fourth), f\"{fourth}: holds ['extra.html', 'index.html', 'manifest.json', 'release-data.json'], \"\n   829\t                                                \"not exactly ['index.html', 'manifest.json', 'release-data.json']\")\n   830\t\n   831\t\n   832\tCERTIFIED_TEMPLATE_SHA256 = 'f94bb3cbf5ba1030ee37f0111b78bf2e58f7f767d77aa7e7d2443677e5811ae2'   # certified by poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b\n   833\t\n   834\t\n   835\tdef test_29_the_page_template_is_the_one_the_screen_run_certified():\n   836\t    \"\"\"RELEASE-PAGE.md revision 7, test 3: the whole page template, with its data placeholder, is the one the $0 screen run certified\n   837\t    (poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b); any change to any part of it fails here until a new screen run certifies it.\"\"\"\n   838\t    assert hashlib.sha256(release.page_template().encode('utf-8')).hexdigest() == CERTIFIED_TEMPLATE_SHA256\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '480,515p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md | sed -n '1,27p;94,150p;211,261p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '480,515p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md | sed -n '1,27p;94,150p;211,261p'\"","aggregated_output":"   480\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\n   481\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \"Bullish\", is recorded as such.\n   482\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\n   483\t\n   484\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\n   485\t\n   486\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\n   487\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \"more than $40 billion in\n   488\tFY2028\" for a quote's \"more than double that next year\".\n   489\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\n   490\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\n   491\t  sentence. One restates \"close to doubling\" as \"nearly 100%\".\n   492\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\n   493\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \"takes\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\n   494\t  judged position.\n   495\t- **Council 74b** (`codex-r74b.md` §2) verified that extraction sends no rung, label or judged position, and that the census\n   496\t  reproduces.\n   497\t- **The disagreement that remains is narrow.**\n   498\t  - Codex reads revision 4's \"amounts as quoted\" as requiring source wording for a calculated amount attributed to a source, such\n   499\t    as `e3238`'s \"more than $40 billion\".\n   500\t  - Claude reads it as \"the release computes or converts nothing\".\n   501\t  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\n   502\t- **The course taken.** By AGENTS' rule for an unsettled disagreement, the cheaper, reversible course is to keep the stored summary.\n   503\t  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\n   504\t  allow-list or change it.\n     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" release, slice 2: the reader's page (design for council round 76)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Status: revision 7, ready per council 76h; built and screen-checked** (`RELEASE-PAGE-RESULT.md`; build review in council 77).\n     4\tDuring the build, the evidence detail line was changed to add \", <day>\" only when the original day exists. The template was\n     5\tre-certified by a new screen run and its hash re-pinned.\n     6\t\n     7\t**Revision 7 answers `codex-r76g.md`:**\n     8\t- **Contrast starts at the text's own element.** Its background is its own non-transparent `background-color`, or else the nearest\n     9\t  ancestor's. A marker with dark text on its own dark background inside a light card fails.\n    10\t- **The whole template is pinned.** `page_template()` is the complete page text with the CSP filled and one data placeholder;\n    11\t  `render_page` splits it at that placeholder and inserts the escaped data. The test pins the sha256 of `page_template()`, so a\n    12\t  change to any part of the page, the fallback sentence included, fails the pin until re-certified.\n    13\t\n    14\tCouncil 76g judged further checks against hypothetical CSS optional once these are in: a template change already fails the pin.\n    15\t\n    16\t**Revision 6 answers `codex-r76f.md` with general rules instead of one patch per trick** (AGENTS §1: \"certify what the reader can\n    17\tread\" drew a new finding in 76c, 76d and 76f):\n    18\t1. **No clipping ancestor.** No element between a read text and `body` may clip it: computed `overflow-x` or `overflow-y` other than\n    19\t   `visible`, `contain` holding `paint`, `strict` or `content`, or `clip-path` other than `none`.\n    20\t2. **Contrast.** Every read text has a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 between its computed colour and its effective background (the\n    21\t   nearest ancestor with a non-transparent background), in light and in dark. This is WCAG's AA level for body text.\n    22\t3. **The template is pinned.** The sha256 of `PAGE_STYLE` and `PAGE_SCRIPT` are literals in the tests. The screen check certifies\n    23\t   that exact template, and any template change fails the tests until it is re-certified by a new screen run and a new format\n    24\t   version.\n    25\t\n    26\t**Revision 5 answers `codex-r76d.md`:** no text may be clipped.\n    27\t- The template's stylesheet uses none of `overflow`, `clip`, `text-overflow`, `line-clamp`, `max-height` or `nowrap`.\n    94\t    hold no `</script` and no `<!--`.\n    95\t  - **The file starts** with `<!doctype html>`, then `<meta charset=\"utf-8\">`, then the CSP `<meta>`, before any style, script or\n    96\t    data.\n    97\t  - **A Content-Security-Policy `<meta>`:**\n    98\t    `default-src 'none'; script-src 'sha256-<inline script>'; style-src 'sha256-<inline style>'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none';\n    99\t    connect-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'`. The two hashes are computed from the template's own script and style,\n   100\t    so the browser refuses any other script, style or connection.\n   101\t  - **The script** builds the page only with `document.createElement`, `textContent` and `className`. It creates no `<a>` element,\n   102\t    no `href` and no `src`. It never uses `innerHTML`, `outerHTML`, `insertAdjacentHTML`, `document.write`, `eval`, `Function`, or any network API\n   103\t    (`fetch`, `XMLHttpRequest`, `WebSocket`, `EventSource`, `navigator.sendBeacon`, `import()`, `Worker`).\n   104\t  - **The style** uses system fonts and inline colour tokens copied from `web/design-system/tokens.css`. It generates no text: no\n   105\t    `content` property anywhere, so every word a reader sees is a text node the screen check can read. It clips no text: none of\n   106\t    `overflow`, `clip`, `text-overflow`, `line-clamp`, `max-height` or `white-space: nowrap`, and long words wrap\n   107\t    (`overflow-wrap: anywhere`). It has a dark scheme under\n   108\t    `prefers-color-scheme: dark`, and it works at phone width.\n   109\t- **`write_package`** also writes `index.html = render_page(data bytes)` and records its sha256.\n   110\t- **`check_package`** also:\n   111\t  - reads `index.html` once through the same folder handle;\n   112\t  - requires its bytes to equal `render_page(the data bytes it read)` exactly;\n   113\t  - requires the manifest's `page_sha256` to match.\n   114\t\n   115\t  A page that differs by one byte from the function of the data is refused. So a page cannot carry anything the data does not hold,\n   116\t  and no code the template does not hold.\n   117\t\n   118\t**What the page shows,** in package order. Each shown value sits in an element with a fixed class, so the screen check can read it:\n   119\t`question-text`, `question-status`, `question-forecast`, `question-answer`, `evidence-count`, `evidence-summary`, `evidence-quote`,\n   120\t`evidence-meta`, `source-title`, `source-publisher`, `source-day`, `source-address`.\n   121\t- **A header:** \"Hivemind release\", the package's day, and the count of questions by class.\n   122\t- **Each question:**\n   123\t  - its question text and \"Open\" or \"Closed\";\n   124\t  - for a number question, the marker \"Forecast unavailable\";\n   125\t  - for an event or Yes/No question, \"Answer: <label>\", or \"Not yet answered\" when the answer is null;\n   126\t  - \"<n> pieces of evidence\", and a `<details>` element. When opened, it builds the evidence list:\n   127\t    - each piece shows its summary, the quote, and a line with tier, speaker, and original speaker and day;\n   128\t    - each source shows title, publisher, day and its address as plain text. The page has no links, so neither a click nor a script\n   129\t      can make a request (council 76).\n   130\t\n   131\t  Evidence is built only when opened, so the first screen stays fast on a 6 MB package.\n   132\t\n   133\t## 2. State × event (the page and the check)\n   134\t\n   135\t| State / event | What happens |\n   136\t|---|---|\n   137\t| Package with no questions | \"No questions as of <day>\" |\n   138\t| A question with no evidence | \"No evidence in force\", and no `<details>` |\n   139\t| A source address of any scheme, `javascript:` included | shown as text; the page has no links |\n   140\t| Text holding `</script>`, `<img onerror=…>`, `&` or U+2028 | the embed escapes it, the page shows it as text, and the JSON parses back identical |\n   141\t| The page is opened from disk, a static host or any path | it reads only its embedded data; nothing else exists to read |\n   142\t| The browser blocks the inline script | the fallback line stays visible; nothing else renders, and the page holds no forecast to leak |\n   143\t| A page edited after the build (a fetch added, a field added) | `check_package` refuses: the bytes differ from `render_page(data)` |\n   144\t| The template changes in a later version | old packages fail `check_package` under the new code by design; a new template is a new format version |\n   145\t| A dark scheme and a phone width | checked in §6: at 390 px wide the page has no horizontal scroll; with the dark scheme emulated, the body's background is the dark token |\n   146\t\n   147\t## 3. Value × reader\n   148\t\n   149\t- Every value the page shows comes from the embedded data; the page reads no other value.\n   150\t- The page's readers are a person's browser and the browser check.\n   211\t- a `Log.entryAdded` error;\n   212\t- a `Runtime.exceptionThrown`;\n   213\t- a `Runtime.consoleAPICalled` of type `error`.\n   214\t\n   215\t**Expected values, frozen before the run.** `release_screen.mjs` reads `screen-expected.json`. It is written before the first screen\n   216\trun, with its sha256 recorded in the result, from the accepted slice-1 packages:\n   217\t- `poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-1/package` for `v8`;\n   218\t- `old-3/package-2026-08-25` for `old-3/v36` (at that day it asks whether NVIDIA will begin shipping Rubin Ultra);\n   219\t- `old-1/package-2026-08-28` for `old-1/v10`.\n   220\t\n   221\tFor each checked page it holds the page's complete visible text:\n   222\t- **the header:** \"Hivemind release\", \"As of <day>\", and the counts line;\n   223\t- **every card collapsed,** in package order: its id, then its question, status, the marker or the answer, and the evidence count\n   224\t  (or \"No evidence in force\");\n   225\t- **the checked card expanded:** for each evidence entry in order, its own group: summary, quote, meta line, and per source its\n   226\t  title, publisher, day and address.\n   227\t\n   228\t**How the page is read.**\n   229\t- **What counts as visible.** The check walks every text node of `document.body` in document order. It keeps a text only when its\n   230\t  element passes `checkVisibility({opacityProperty: true, visibilityProperty: true, contentVisibilityAuto: true})` and has a\n   231\t  non-zero box. A text inside a transparent, hidden or collapsed ancestor is not visible.\n   232\t- **Not clipped.**\n   233\t  - For each kept text whose element is a block (not `display: inline`), the element's `scrollWidth` is at most `clientWidth + 1` and\n   234\t    its `scrollHeight` at most `clientHeight + 1`.\n   235\t  - No ancestor between it and `body` clips: none has `overflow-x` or `overflow-y` other than `visible`, `contain` holding `paint`,\n   236\t    `strict` or `content`, or `clip-path` other than `none`.\n   237\t  - Any clipped text fails the page, whatever its content.\n   238\t- **Readable.** Each kept text's contrast ratio is at least 4.5:1, computed (WCAG relative luminance) between its element's computed\n   239\t  `color` and the first non-transparent `background-color` found from that element itself upward, the page canvas if none. This is checked in light and in\n   240\t  dark. Any text below the ratio fails the page.\n   241\t- **Where each text goes:** to the header, to a card (by `data-id`), to an evidence group within a card, or else to `other`.\n   242\t  `other` must be empty.\n   243\t- **What must match.** The read page must equal the frozen page exactly: collapsed, then with the checked card expanded, then after\n   244\t  closing and reopening it.\n   245\t- **What that catches.** An extra visible line anywhere fails: inside the card, beside it, or in the header. For example,\n   246\t  \"Forecast: $361 billion\", Morningstar's genuine figure shown as if it were the system's. So does a missing, duplicated, regrouped\n   247\t  or reordered entry.\n   248\t\n   249\t**The screen of `old-1/v8`:**\n   250\t- **Collapsed:** the whole read page equals the frozen page. The `v8` card reads \"How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA\n   251\t  report for FY2027?\", \"Open\", \"Forecast unavailable\", \"1284 pieces of evidence\".\n   252\t- **With `v8` expanded:** the whole read page equals the frozen page with `v8`'s 1,284 groups. The full Morningstar quote and its\n   253\t  attribution are included, and \"Bullish\" appears only where a frozen source text holds it.\n   254\t- **Closed and reopened once:** the same.\n   255\t- **No link anywhere on the page:** zero `a` elements, zero `[href]`, zero `[src]`.\n   256\t- **A screenshot** of the expanded card's top is saved with the result.\n   257\t\n   258\t**The leak screens.** For `old-3/v36` at 2026-08-25 and `old-1/v10` at 2026-08-28:\n   259\t- the page's day equals its package's;\n   260\t- the whole read page, collapsed and with the card expanded, equals the frozen page from that dated package. The card holds its\n   261\t  question, status, \"Answer: Yes\", \"1 piece of evidence\", then its single evidence entry and source;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
