{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'as quoted|calculat|conver|summar|arithmet' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/{FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN,codex-r74b,codex-r74c}.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:14:- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:49:  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:60:  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.md:14:### 2. The evidence-summary disagreement\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.md:16:**Yes, §8 records it faithfully.** In `e3238`, the source says “more than double” a $20 billion figure. The stored summary attributes “more than $40 billion” to NVIDIA. Both readers agree the arithmetic is faithful and the figure did not come from Hivemind’s judgement. They disagree on whether “amounts as quoted” permits that attribution. Section 8 preserves both readings and identifies keeping the summary alongside the quote as the cheaper, reversible decision. The reported percentages count extra digit sequences across evidence records. They do not establish how often a calculated amount is attributed to a source. [codex-r74b.md:18](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:18) · [codex-r74b.md:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:20) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:362](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:362)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74c.md:23:- **Run test 12 through the real builder on a scratch copy.** Establish that the unchanged command succeeds. On the scratch copy, introduce the already-listed writer fault that substitutes judgement text for one evidence summary. Run the same command and require the origin-mismatch reason, nonzero exit, no output package and removal of its staging folder. Then remove only the staged check while retaining the writer fault. The bad package must reach the destination and make the refusal test fail. This proves exactly which check prevents publication, using the mutation procedure AGENTS §4 already specifies. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:282](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:282) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:296](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:296) · [AGENTS.md:158](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:158)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:1:**Verdict: not ready to build.** The revised check would catch Hivemind’s $390 billion forecast substituted into Morningstar’s summary. It could still certify `old-1` as current through September 21, although the store’s last completed day is September 20. It could also certify `old-1/v10` with its real “Yes” answer replaced by “Forecast unavailable.” Both errors survive because the checker takes the date and question type from the package it is checking. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:88](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:88) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:172](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:172) · [service.py:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:64)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:14:### 2. Disputed evidence summaries\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:18:**The census percentages reproduce.** The counts are 1,379/5,390, 1,284/5,102, 1,386/5,447 and 1,470/4,199. They measure extra digit sequences across distinct evidence records linked to **all** question types. A year, `H200`, and a calculated dollar amount all count. The sample was six flagged records per store. This supplies evidence against filtering every numeric mismatch. It does not measure how often a summary attributes a calculated amount to a source. [oneline_census.py:5](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/oneline_census.py:5) · [oneline_census.py:18](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/oneline_census.py:18) · [claude-r74.md:42](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md:42)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:20:**I still disagree on “amounts as quoted.”** Keeping `e3238` does not disclose a D726 judgement. But I read the underlying article: it says `$20 billion` and “more than double that next year.” The stored summary says **NVIDIA projected more than $40 billion**. The arithmetic is faithful. The attributed dollar figure is extraction’s wording. Revision 4 explicitly requires “amounts as quoted,” so I would use the source wording for that amount. The disagreement is narrow and does not justify a digit filter or a change to extraction. Under the stated council fallback, keeping the stored summary is the cheaper reversible course, with this exception recorded. This dispute is separate from the build blockers. [FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:47](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:47) · [DECISIONS-log.md:11004](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11004) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:296](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:296)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
