{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b --no-ignore | head -20\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE-RESULT.md | sed -n '70,92p'\"","aggregated_output":"poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1-0828.report.json\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-expected.json\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-3-0825.report.json\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/mutant-line-beside/index.html\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/mutant-line-inside/index.html\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/mutant-fetch/index.html\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/mutant-clipped/index.html\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1/release-data.json\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1/manifest.json\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1/index.html\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-3-0825/release-data.json\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-3-0825/manifest.json\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-3-0825/index.html\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/escape.report.json\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/mutant-unreadable-marker/index.html\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1.report.json\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1-0828/release-data.json\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1-0828/manifest.json\npoc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1-0828/index.html\n    70\texpectation: zero failures. The browser profile now lives outside the run folder. The profiles of earlier runs were moved to the\n    71\tscratchpad, not deleted.\n    72\t\n    73\t**Measured, recorded in the design:** Chrome reports a CSP-blocked fetch as two log errors, not as a network request. A scratchpad\n    74\tprobe page named port 8788 once. Chrome refused it under the CSP before connecting, so nothing reached that service.\n    75\t\n    76\t## 3. One change during the build\n    77\t\n    78\t- **What.** The first screenshot showed a dangling comma when a source has no original day (\"original: NVIDIA,\"). The page now adds\n    79\t  \", <day>\" only when there is a day.\n    80\t- **How it was re-certified.** That changed the pinned template, so the expectation was frozen again in a new folder\n    81\t  (`release-screen-2026-11-23b`), the screen check re-run (zero failures, all eight negatives caught), and the new template hash\n    82\t  pinned (`f94bb3cb…`, test 29).\n    83\t\n    84\t**A pre-release departure, recorded (council 77).** The comma change altered the template under the same format 2, where revision 7\n    85\tsays a changed template gets a new format version. The earlier page was never released, and the current checker refuses it. The\n    86\tformat-version rule applies from the first release on.\n    87\t\n    88\t## 4. Not shown, and still open\n    89\t\n    90\t- **The idea path in the release** (council 74): deferred, its acceptance pending.\n    91\t- **The evidence-summary disagreement** (`RELEASE-BUILD.md` §8): recorded, with the cheaper course taken.\n    92\t- **Commit, publish and deploy:** Alex's.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'amounts as quoted|no conversion|compute.*amount|as.*source|source wording' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs | sed -n '87,113p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'amounts as quoted|no conversion|compute.*amount|as.*source|source wording' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74.md\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs | sed -n '87,113p'\"","aggregated_output":"1:**Verdict: not ready to build.** The proposed check would accept Hivemind’s own forecast inside an allowed text field. It would also flag genuine source material. Both failures are reproducible on `old-1/v8`: the check misses the stored forecast of about **$390 billion**, while a source quote legitimately contains the withheld label **“Bullish.”** [Release check:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:197) · [Evidence returned to the exporter:232](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:232)\n12:| `old-1/v8/e5309` | The source title forecasts **$31.6 trillion** of global spending by 2050. The linked evidence concerns NVIDIA’s reported first-half revenue. The title is a publisher’s forecast and belongs with its source. |\n14:The writer checks the quote against the article. It stores the generated `one_line` separately. Linking the two to a number question establishes neither that every amount was quoted nor that the summary contains a Hivemind judgement. Keep attributed source forecasts and the original question. For the release promise of “amounts as quoted,” use the source wording where the summary introduces a calculated figure. Verify each exported value against its designated origin. A valid key name alone cannot establish that origin. [Signed design:47](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:47) · [Quote check:671](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:671) · [Evidence writer:29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:29) · [Question writer:38](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:38)\n20:| State × event | **Missing source item.** `item_lookup` substitutes the input ID for the title and empty strings for publisher and URI. All pass the proposed string checks. Refuse a visible source that cannot be matched to its item. The four store/item pairs I checked had zero missing source IDs. [Lookup:28](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:28) · [Proposed value checks:62](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:62) |\n32:- **Tests 1, 2 and 7** catch an extra key or a copied passage. Add a mutant that keeps every key valid and puts the number judgement into `one_line`. Exercise the exporter through the builder. Check the exact source-backed value and confirm a refused build produces no final package. Calling `check_export` on an edited dictionary alone does not exercise the writer’s refusal. [Tests:163](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:163) · [Writer requirement:124](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:124)\n38:**Reject the 12-character floor as a release gate.** On `old-1/v8` it skips three of five labels: `Bullish`, `Neutral` and `Bearish`. Removing the floor still gives a wrong result. `old-1/v8/e1865` genuinely begins its source quote with **“Bullish confirmation would require…”**. Section 7’s requirement that none of the five labels occur anywhere conflicts with preserving that quote. [Sweep and acceptance:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:197)\n40:I also checked the opposite error in memory. The **entire** `old-1/v8/j1580.implied_outcome`, beginning “About $390 billion,” contains **zero** of §7’s searched strings of 12 or more characters. The restatement “Our estimate for the year is $390bn” also produces zero. The sweep omits `implied_outcome`, `reference`, numeric bounds and structured judgement values. Searching serialized JSON also changes how quotation marks and newlines appear. Use exact matches on **decoded fields** as diagnostics, including short labels. Make the pass condition an independent comparison of package fields with their permitted source values at the requested date. Preserve the genuine $390 billion article quote in `old-1/e3597` as the control. [Stored judgement fields:18](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/store.py:18) · [Proposed sweep:201](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:201)\n49:| Sweep floor | **Remove it as a safety criterion.** Keep diagnostic hits attributable to a particular question, field and source. [Release check:197](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:197) |\n    87\t  const lum = ({ r, g, b }) => { const f = (x) => { x /= 255; return x <= 0.03928 ? x / 12.92 : ((x + 0.055) / 1.055) ** 2.4; }; return 0.2126 * f(r) + 0.7152 * f(g) + 0.0722 * f(b); };\n    88\t  const background = (e) => { for (let a = e; a; a = a.parentElement) { const c = rgb(getComputedStyle(a).backgroundColor); if (c && c.a > 0) return c; } return rgb(getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).backgroundColor) || { r: 255, g: 255, b: 255, a: 1 }; };\n    89\t  const contrast = (e) => { const f = lum(rgb(getComputedStyle(e).color)), b = lum(background(e)); return (Math.max(f, b) + 0.05) / (Math.min(f, b) + 0.05); };\n    90\t  const clippingAncestor = (e) => { for (let a = e.parentElement; a && a !== document.body; a = a.parentElement) { const s = getComputedStyle(a);\n    91\t    if (s.overflowX !== 'visible' || s.overflowY !== 'visible' || /paint|strict|content/.test(s.contain) || s.clipPath !== 'none') return true; } return false; };\n    92\t  const byId = new Map();\n    93\t  const walker = document.createTreeWalker(document.body, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);\n    94\t  for (let n = walker.nextNode(); n; n = walker.nextNode()) {\n    95\t    const text = n.textContent.trim();\n    96\t    const owner = n.parentElement;\n    97\t    if (!text || !owner || owner.closest('script') || !visible(owner)) continue;\n    98\t    if ((getComputedStyle(owner).display !== 'inline' && (owner.scrollWidth > owner.clientWidth + 1 || owner.scrollHeight > owner.clientHeight + 1)) || clippingAncestor(owner)) {\n    99\t      page.clipped.push(text.slice(0, 80));\n   100\t    }\n   101\t    if (contrast(owner) < 4.5) page.unreadable.push(text.slice(0, 80));\n   102\t    const card = owner.closest('article.question');\n   103\t    if (owner.closest('header.release-header')) { page.header.push(text); continue; }\n   104\t    if (!card) { page.other.push(text); continue; }\n   105\t    let entry = byId.get(card.dataset.id);\n   106\t    if (!entry) { entry = { id: card.dataset.id, top: [], groups: [] }; byId.set(card.dataset.id, entry); page.cards.push(entry); }\n   107\t    const item = owner.closest('li.evidence-item');\n   108\t    if (!item) { entry.top.push(text); continue; }\n   109\t    const index = [...card.querySelectorAll('li.evidence-item')].indexOf(item);\n   110\t    while (entry.groups.length <= index) entry.groups.push([]);\n   111\t    entry.groups[index].push(text);\n   112\t  }\n   113\t  for (const entry of page.cards) entry.groups = entry.groups.filter((g) => g.length);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
