{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'pre.release|first release|format.version rule|unreleased|new format' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r77*.md docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -22 | cut -c1-1800\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r77b.md:11:The **one product departure** is the documented comma correction under the same format number. Revision 7 calls for a new format when the template changes. The earlier and final manifests have identical data hashes and different page hashes. I checked that the current checker refuses the earlier page and accepts the final one. This was a pre-release versioning departure with no observed reader-safety impact. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:144) · [Earlier manifest:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23/old-1/manifest.json:1) · [Final manifest:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1/manifest.json:1)\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r77.md:7:One harmless pre-release departure is worth recording. Both versions of the page use format 2, although revision 7 says a changed template gets a new format. The comma correction changed the page hash while the data hash stayed identical. I confirmed that the current checker refuses the earlier page and accepts the final one. The browser profile also lives in the run folder instead of the specified scratchpad, outside the release package. [Design:144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:144) · [Earlier manifest:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23/old-1/manifest.json:1) · [Final manifest:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1/manifest.json:1) · [Browser setup:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:40)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10829:  - 先停在这里 (recommended: poc-v118 stays; the new format's code is kept but not enabled; no further spend);\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10986:- **Interim for a first release:** number questions shown as \"Forecast unavailable\" until they pass the checks.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11004:  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11799:## D755 · 2026-11-23 · The paid re-send STOPs (complete); council 71: close v13s at STOP and carry D726's \"Forecast unavailable\" into the first release\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11814:  - the first release carries D726: number questions show their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with the range, forecast text and\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833:  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \"Forecast unavailable\", the band, the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11972:- **Pre-release departure (council 77):** the comma fix changed the template under the same format 2. The earlier page was never\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
