{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11965,11980p'\nwc -l poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-1/package/release-data.json\nrg -n 'e3238' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r74.md\"","aggregated_output":" 11965\t  - a screen check must read the whole page as the reader sees it: visible, unclipped and readable text, in place;\n 11966\t  - \"certify readability against any CSS\" draws findings without end, so the structural answer is a pinned template certified once;\n 11967\t  - Chrome reports a CSP-blocked fetch as log errors, not as a request.\n 11968\t- **Process slips, recorded:**\n 11969\t  - twice an edit script and its review launch were not chained with `&&`, so round 76e read a stale revision (AGENTS §9);\n 11970\t  - the first screen run passed a relative `file://` path, and the first light check inherited the system's dark scheme. Both were\n 11971\t    found from their outputs and fixed before any result was claimed.\n 11972\t- **Pre-release departure (council 77):** the comma fix changed the template under the same format 2. The earlier page was never\n 11973\t  released, and the current checker refuses it.\n 11974\t- **Still Alex's:**\n 11975\t  - commit, push, publish and deploy;\n 11976\t  - where the release page is served;\n 11977\t  - whether it replaces the page colleagues use;\n 11978\t  - the idea path (needs a running service and a paid model; deferred by council 74).\n       0 poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/old-1/package/release-data.json\n34:`codex-r74.md` §1 asks the release to use the source wording where a summary introduces a calculated figure (`e3238`: \"more than\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"**Verdict: keep the §8 disagreement open.** I support adding “Hivemind summary” and “Source quote.” The first label tells the reader who wrote the sentence. The sentence still tells the reader that NVIDIA projected more than $40 billion. The source expressed that projection as “more than double that next year.” That distinction was the original objection. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:497](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:497) · [codex-r74b.md:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md:20)\n\n1. **What would settle it.** I would agree to a summary that makes clear who did the arithmetic. For example, “NVIDIA projected $20 billion this year and more than double that next year. Hivemind calculates that this implies more than $40 billion.” If the stored sentence must appear verbatim, the other way to settle this is an explicit council decision that “amounts as quoted” applies to the quote alone and that a labelled summary may express a source’s projection in calculated dollars. That would resolve the interpretation directly. Revision 4 currently applies the phrase to the evidence entry as a whole. [FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:47](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:47) · [RELEASE-BUILD.md:486](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:486)\n\n2. **Format.** Keeping `/2` is acceptable before the first release. Revision 7 says a changed template gets a new format, but the accepted build report explicitly says that rule applies **from the first release**. Council 77 already re-certified a changed `/2` page and verified that the checker refused the earlier one. `/3` is valid if the council wants a distinct identifier, but certification alone does not require it. Either choice needs a fresh screen run and a new whole-template pin. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:144) · [RELEASE-PAGE-RESULT.md:80](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE-RESULT.md:80) · [codex-r77b.md:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r77b.md:11)\n\n3. **What the labels could break.**\n   - Put each label in its own visible text element inside the evidence entry, immediately before the text it describes. Keep the quote element’s text exact. Both the phone wrapping check and the escaping check locate a quote by its full text. Two clipping tests also depend on the exact line that creates the quote element. [release.py:519](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:519) · [release_screen.mjs:199](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:199) · [release_screen.mjs:227](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:227) · [release_screen.mjs:274](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:274)\n   - Freeze the expected reading order from the accepted package data before the run. Add both labels to every expanded evidence group on all three checked cards. The collapsed page should read as before, and reopening a card should show each label once per entry. The existing reader checks the labels themselves for 4.5:1 contrast and clipping on the light desktop and 390 px dark phone screens. [release_screen_prepare.py:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen_prepare.py:46) · [release_screen_prepare.py:86](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen_prepare.py:86) · [release_screen.mjs:93](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:93) · [release_screen.mjs:151](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:151) · [release_screen.mjs:194](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:194)\n   - Update the template pin after the screen passes. If `/3` is chosen, the production identifier, package test, and independent release checker each name the format explicitly. [test_release.py:832](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:832) · [release.py:25](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:25) · [test_release.py:210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:210) · [release_check.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:24)\n\n4. **Council record.** Record agreement on the two labels. Keep the narrower question open: may a summary say the source projected a calculated dollar amount when the source gave a comparison? This was a read-only review. No files changed and no new screen result is claimed. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:498](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:498)"}}
